(b)require the consent, as specified in the laws and regulations of that Party, of recipients to receive commercial electronic messages; or(c)otherwise provide for the minimisation of unsolicited commercial electronic messages.2.Each Party shall provide recourse against a supplier of unsolicited commercial electronic messages that does not comply with a measure adopted or maintained in accordance with paragraph 1.3.The Parties shall endeavour to cooperate in appropriate cases of mutual concern regarding the regulation of unsolicited commercial electronic messages.
